From c9443367b5c7ee014311ad507831fba2f3c7ad3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 08:14:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/15] rdna-boosts: block 08: fused-core prefill kernels and
 GPU bit-identical

AMENDED 2026-09-07 (PR #15, reporter DanoPTT): the mul_mat+bias fusion
evaluates ggml_cuda_should_fuse_mul_mat_vec_* on the matmul node but
passes bias_node to the kernel as the destination.  Without a view
between them those are the same tensor, so the guard is sound.  Block
08's "fuse mul_mat + add through a view node" lets a reshape sit
between the two, and a reshape can move tokens across dimensions: with
two sequences in one batch the matmul is ne = [5120,1,2] -- a
single-column GEMV as far as the guard is concerned -- while the add it
feeds is ne = [5120,2,1].  The kernels index the destination by ne[1]/
ne[2] and assert on exactly that (mmvq.cu: GGML_ASSERT(ids ||
dst->ne[1] == 1)).  Require the destination to satisfy the same
constraint the kernels assert before fusing through a view.  The
single-sequence case is unaffected.
Folds beta/mmb-general: 0001 (mmb GEMM core), 0003 (F32/tiny-M kernels + width probe; the
qwen4exp always-QSA flip deferred to block 14), 0006 (RDNA4 fragment port), 0007 (dense tile
geometry + quant coverage), 0008 (per-arch defaults; the HC16 env overrides deferred to block 14),
0009 (routed policy), 0010 (F32 policy split), 0012 (gfx1100 F32 split), 0014 (GDN/PLE conv1d
fusions; the qwen4exp fusion stand-downs deferred to block 13), 0015 (narrow-row RMS norm fusion).
